This is a modified copy of Anthropic's sandbox-runtime (Apache-2.0).

Modification: Added an opt-in network.unrestricted configuration flag and --unrestricted-network CLI flag that bypasses the proxy-based network filter while keeping the filesystem sandbox.

Modification: Linux standalone builds discover apply-seccomp beside the executable. Requested Unix-socket blocking fails closed when the helper is missing or not executable, including when no other restrictions are requested. Existing package-install lookup is preserved.

Distribution: Native macOS and Linux x64/arm64 executables are built and smoke-tested by release-junie.yml. Linux releases include an architecture-matched apply-seccomp helper; bubblewrap, socat and ripgrep remain system dependencies. See docs/jetbrains-build.md for the tested baseline and THIRD-PARTY for bundled dependency notices.

